1. DERIVATION — WMLST IS A DERIVATIVE WORK, NOT AN ORIGINAL ONE
================================================================================

WMLST is a port to Python/Windows of:

    mlst 2.35.0
    Copyright (C) Torsten Seemann
    https://github.com/tseemann/mlst
    Licensed under the GNU General Public License version 2, June 1991,
    WITHOUT an "or (at your option) any later version" clause.

A port is a translation. Under GPLv2 section 0 a translation is a modification,
so WMLST is unambiguously a work based on the Program. Under GPLv2 section 2(b)
the derivative must be licensed as a whole at no charge under the same terms.
WMLST therefore is, and can only be, GPL-2.0-only. It is not dual-licensed; the
newly written parts are not MIT; "GPLv2 for the ported parts" is not a thing.

The following modules are direct, line-by-line translations of upstream Perl and
carry an SPDX header naming the upstream file and line range they came from:

    wmlst/engine.py     <- bin/mlst, perl5/MLST/*.pm
    wmlst/schemes.py    <- perl5/MLST/Scheme.pm, perl5/MLST/SchemeDb.pm
    wmlst/any2fasta.py  <- any2fasta 0.9.0 by Torsten Seemann (GPL-3.0 upstream;
                           see section 5 below for why this is compatible here)
    the BLAST database builder in wmlst/updatedb.py
                        <- scripts/mlst-make_blast_db

Please cite the original author first. Without Torsten Seemann's work there is
nothing here to port.

    Seemann T, mlst, https://github.com/tseemann/mlst

