3. NCBI BLAST+ — NOT BUNDLED IN THE SOURCE TREE
================================================================================

WMLST calls blastn and makeblastdb from NCBI BLAST+ 2.17.0.

    NCBI BLAST+ is a "United States Government Work". It is in the PUBLIC DOMAIN
    within the United States and carries no copyright restriction. NCBI makes no
    warranty as to its accuracy or fitness for any purpose.
    https://blast.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/
    Altschul SF, Gish W, Miller W, Myers EW, Lipman DJ (1990)
    "Basic local alignment search tool." J Mol Biol 215:403-410.

The git repository does NOT contain BLAST+ binaries. On Windows, `wmlst
--bootstrap-blast` (or the GUI's first-run prompt) downloads the official NCBI
archive over HTTPS, verifies its MD5, and extracts only blastn.exe,
makeblastdb.exe and nghttp2.dll into

    %LOCALAPPDATA%\IOWA-BioTech\WMLST\blast\

Because BLAST+ is public domain, distributing those binaries alongside a GPLv2
program raises no licence conflict; they are also merely invoked as separate
processes, never linked.

The Windows installer and the portable zip produced by packaging/wmlst.iss and
packaging/wmlst.spec DO include those three files together with the NCBI LICENSE
and BLAST_PRIVACY notices, which are installed into {app}\blast\.

