4. OTHER COMPONENTS
================================================================================

tkinterdnd2 (OPTIONAL, GUI drag-and-drop only)
    MIT licence. Imported behind a try/except ImportError; WMLST degrades to a
    Browse button when it is absent. MIT is GPLv2-compatible.

PyInstaller (BUILD TIME ONLY, never shipped as a library)
    GPLv2 with the standard bootloader exception, which explicitly permits
    freezing applications of any licence. Only the bootloader it generates is
    redistributed, under that exception.

Inno Setup (BUILD TIME ONLY)
    Its own permissive licence; the generated installer imposes no terms.

Python standard library
    PSF Licence Agreement, GPL-compatible.

WMLST has ZERO mandatory third-party runtime dependencies, and that is a licence
decision as much as a packaging one: a GPLv2 program cannot link an Apache-2.0
library, because Apache 2.0's patent-termination clause imposes a restriction
GPLv2 section 6 forbids. Adding any runtime dependency to this project therefore
requires a licence review, and scripts/check_stdlib_only.py enforces the rule in
CI.

================================================================================
5. A NOTE ON any2fasta
================================================================================

Upstream mlst shells out to any2fasta 0.9.0, a separate GPL-3.0 program by the
same author. WMLST does not ship, link to, or execute that program: wmlst/
any2fasta.py is an independent Python implementation of the same conversions,
written against the documented behaviour and the observable output, and carries
the GPL-2.0-only header of this project like every other file. No GPL-3.0 code
is incorporated, so no GPLv2/GPLv3 incompatibility arises.

